valueSha256 be9da085… equals sha256('[masked]'), the literal placeholder in the SA-ADR72 log line 'postgres://mth_app:[masked]@…'. It is not a credential.

The entry is scopes: ['history'] only. In history scope, secret-scan.mjs l.382 ignores the path, so the entry exempts an S2 password exactly equal to '[masked]' anywhere in history. That is harmless (no real password can hide behind it), and it never applies to the payload.

