Cause: backup.sh l.446 writes the list to the database phase's $WORK (l.311), which its EXIT trap removes (l.319); l.585 reads it from the finish phase's new $WORK. This is F-DG7-1071 (Medium).

The grant is least privilege:
- read/search only, no DAC_OVERRIDE, so it cannot write the 10001-owned store;
- one-off `run --rm` with a fixed entrypoint;
- root writes only into its own 0700 set.

It is documented in the guide (§3.2 'Why root, and why one capability'). However, ADR-0066 has no mention of it, of DATABASE_URL_FILE or of the /mth/deploy layout. A1.4 still says the Compose run was not executed. decisions.md has 0 DAC_READ_SEARCH mentions, so DO-D13 Q2 (architect acceptance) is unanswered. This is documentation drift with no behavioural effect: F-DG7-1073 (Low, non-blocking).
